## The 2ct Breakpoint

![Lab grown radiant cut diamond — The 2ct Breakpoint savings visualization 1ct through 4ct](/images/lab-grown-radiant-cut-2ct-breakpoint.avif)

The 2ct Breakpoint is the carat size where lab grown radiant cuts shift from "good value" to "transformational value." Below 2ct, the savings is significant. At 2ct and above, the savings unlocks a completely different tier of stone than your budget could otherwise reach.

Here is the savings data by carat weight:

| Carat | Lab Price | Natural Comparable | Savings | Savings % |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1ct | [$867 (E-VVS1)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$2,318 (G-VS2)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $1,451 | 63% |
| 1.5ct | [$1,510 (F-VVS1)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29569681?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$7,704 (G-VS2)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29651855?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $6,194 | 80% |
| 2ct | [$2,169 (F-VVS1)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27801066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$17,714 (D-VS2)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16750163?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $15,545 | 88% |
| 2.5ct | [$4,745 (D-VVS1)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28041707?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$29,536 (G-VS2)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/22603770?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $24,791 | 84% |
| 3ct | [$5,350 (D-VVS1)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929424?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | [$44,994 (G-VS1)](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29205249?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | $39,644 | 88% |

The savings percentage doesn't change dramatically after 2ct — it stays around 84–88%. But the absolute dollar figure grows with every half-carat. At 3ct, you save nearly $40,000. That is not a buying decision; it is a life decision.

The practical implication: buyers who had budgeted for a 1ct natural can reach 2ct+ lab for roughly the same money. A buyer with a $5,000 stone budget who planned to buy 1.5ct natural G-VS2 can buy a 3ct lab D-VVS1 for [$5,350](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929424?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — the same budget, twice the carat weight, dramatically better specs.

