## 3 Carat: Lab Grown vs Natural Radiant Head-to-Head

![Lab grown vs natural radiant cut diamond specs at 3 carats — certified price and quality comparison](/images/lab-grown-vs-natural-radiant-3ct-comparison.avif)

The 3ct comparison is the most requested data point for lab vs natural radiant buyers. This is the carat size where the savings becomes a genuinely life-changing number.

**Natural 3ct radiant G-VS1:** [$44,994](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29205249?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). GIA certified. G color — near-colorless. VS1 clarity — eye clean. Full ring with the [Classic Four Prong Platinum setting at $1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational): **$46,174**.

**Lab grown 3ct radiant D-VVS1:** [$5,350](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929424?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). IGI certified. D color — colorless, the highest grade. VVS1 clarity — virtually flawless. Same ring in platinum: **[$6,530](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**.

The lab stone beats the natural stone on both color and clarity — D-VVS1 vs G-VS1. And it costs $39,644 less. The natural stone has no optical advantage whatsoever at these specs. The only thing the natural stone has that the lab does not is geological origin and the associated resale value story.

**What $46,174 buys in natural:** A 3ct G-VS1 radiant ring.
**What $46,174 buys in lab grown:** A 3ct D-VVS1 radiant ring ($6,530) plus an additional $39,644 for literally anything else — a down payment, a trip, an investment account, a second property.

That is the honest 3ct comparison. Neither choice is wrong — they serve different buyers. But the financial picture needs to be stated clearly.

**A note on natural vs lab certification at 3ct.** Natural 3ct radiant cuts are typically GIA certified. Lab grown 3ct radiant cuts are most commonly IGI certified, which has rigorous grading standards. GIA-certified lab stones exist at higher prices. If GIA certification specifically matters to you, the [3ct D-VVS1 IGI at $5,350](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929424?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is graded by the same strict methodology as GIA — IGI's lab diamond grading is industry-standard and widely accepted by insurers, appraisers, and retailers.

