## 4 Carat Lab Grown Radiant Cut: What to Know

A 4ct lab grown radiant cut diamond ring starts at [$7,956](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) with the Knife Edge Solitaire — [$7,031](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) stone plus [$925](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) setting. A D-VVS1 IGI certified 4ct lab radiant diamond ring for under $8,000 is not a typo. It is the current certified market.

**Face-up size at 4ct.** A 4ct radiant cut measures approximately 9.5mm × 8.5mm (elongated) or 9.0mm × 9.0mm (square) depending on L/W ratio. This is a commanding presence on the hand — visible from across a room, obvious as a statement piece, impossible to overlook.

**Setting considerations at 4ct.** A heavier stone needs a setting that can support it. The [Classic Four Prong Platinum Solitaire at $1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the right choice at 4ct — platinum is harder than gold, holds prongs more securely over decades of daily wear, and provides the structural support a large stone requires. At this carat weight, don't cut corners on the setting.

**4ct lab price vs 4ct natural.** Natural 4ct radiant cut diamonds in the GIA-certified G-VS2 range run $80,000–$120,000 depending on proportions. The lab [D-VVS1 IGI at $7,031](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) saves you $75,000+ while delivering better specs. No natural 4ct radiant cut at $7,031 exists.

> "A 4ct lab radiant at $7,031 is the most dramatic example of the value inversion in this market. A natural 4ct radiant at equivalent specs doesn't exist below $80,000. I show buyers this comparison and they often need a moment — because the math is so stark it feels like an error. It isn't. These are certified, real diamonds at current market prices." — Farzana Hasan, **[Diamond Critics](/about-farzana/)**

