## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is a lab grown radiant cut diamond?

A lab grown radiant cut diamond is a real diamond — chemically and physically identical to a mined diamond — grown in a laboratory using HPHT or CVD methods, then cut into the 70-facet radiant cut shape. It carries the same fire, hardness, and refractive index as a natural radiant cut. The only difference is origin: lab, not earth.

### Is a lab grown radiant cut diamond real?

Yes. It is a real diamond. Lab grown diamonds are not simulants like CZ or moissanite — they are actual diamond crystal, carbon bonded in the same cubic structure as natural diamonds. GIA and IGI certify them using the same grading standards. Even trained gemologists cannot distinguish lab from natural without spectrometer testing.

### How much does a lab grown radiant cut diamond cost?

At 1ct, [E-VVS1 IGI starts at $867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). At 2ct, [F-VVS1 IGI starts at $2,169](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27801066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). At 3ct, [D-VVS1 IGI starts at $5,350](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929424?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). At 4ct, [D-VVS1 IGI starts at $7,031](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Entry complete ring: 1ct lab + [Knife Edge Solitaire](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = [$1,792](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

### What is the difference between natural and lab grown radiant cut diamonds?

Origin, price, and resale value. The diamond itself — chemistry, hardness, cut, sparkle — is identical. Natural radiant cuts are earth-mined; lab grown are grown in a facility. Natural costs 63–88% more at the same carat and quality. Natural has modest resale value; lab grown currently has minimal resale market. Both are real diamonds with real certification.

### What clarity should I buy for a lab grown radiant cut?

VS2 minimum, VVS preferred. Most certified lab grown radiant inventory comes VVS1 or VVS2 — the growth environment produces cleaner stones by default. The 70-facet brilliant-cut pattern masks inclusions efficiently. VVS clarity in a lab stone is typically only marginally more expensive than VS2 in the lab market.

### What color should I buy for a lab grown radiant cut diamond?

F or better in any white metal setting. Lab grown D-F pricing is compressed — the price gap between E and D is tiny, and there is almost no financial reason to buy H or I color in a lab stone. In yellow or rose gold, G-H is acceptable; the warm metal absorbs body color.

### How does a 2 carat lab grown radiant cut look?

A 2ct radiant cut measures approximately 7.8mm × 6.5mm (elongated) or 7.0mm × 7.0mm (square), depending on the L/W ratio. Face-up, it reads as a clearly substantial stone — larger than the average engagement diamond, visible as a premium piece. The [2ct F-VVS1 lab at $2,169](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27801066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) produces the same face-up appearance as any natural 2ct radiant of the same proportions.

### Does a lab grown radiant cut have GIA certification?

Lab grown radiant cuts can be IGI, GIA, or GCAL certified. Most certified lab radiant inventory is IGI, which has rigorous lab diamond grading standards. GIA-certified lab diamonds exist but typically at a slight premium. IGI certification is fully accepted by insurers, appraisers, and retailers — it is not a lesser certification for lab stones.

### What setting works best for a lab grown radiant cut engagement ring?

A four-prong setting with a square or rectangular head. The [Knife Edge Solitaire at $925](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) (982 reviews) is the best entry setting. The [Riviera Pavé at $1,500](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/riviera-pave-item-195326?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) adds pavé detail. For 3ct+, the [Classic Four Prong Platinum at $1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) provides lifetime structural durability.

### Is a 3 carat lab grown radiant cut diamond worth it?

Yes — if large carat weight matters to you and resale is not a priority. A [3ct D-VVS1 lab radiant at $5,350](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28929424?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is a certified, real diamond at 88% below the equivalent natural stone. The natural 3ct G-VS1 costs [$44,994](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29205249?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). The lab stone has better color and better clarity. For daily wear on a budget, the lab version is the rational choice.

### How much does a 4 carat lab grown radiant cut diamond ring cost?

Starting at [$7,956](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — [4ct D-VVS1 IGI at $7,031](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) plus the Knife Edge Solitaire at [$925](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/knife-edge-solitaire-by-james-allen-item-316048?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). For 4ct in platinum: [D-VVS1 at $7,031](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27493916?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) + [Classic Four Prong Platinum at $1,180](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) = [$8,211](https://www.bluenile.com/engagement-rings/design-your-own-ring/classic-four-prong-solitaire-engagement-ring-in-platinum-item-194156?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational). Natural 4ct equivalent: $80,000–$120,000.

### Why is a lab grown radiant cut so much cheaper than natural?

Supply mechanics. Natural diamonds formed under specific geological conditions millions of years ago — a finite, constrained supply. Lab grown diamonds are produced on demand as the technology scales. Production efficiency improves continuously, reducing per-carat costs. The diamond itself is identical; the scarcity that drives natural pricing does not apply to lab grown.

### How do I verify a lab grown radiant cut diamond is real?

Check the IGI or GIA certificate. Every certified lab grown diamond has a report number that can be verified on the lab's website. The report confirms carat, color, clarity, cut, and origin ("laboratory grown"). Reputable retailers include the report number in the product listing. If a "lab grown diamond" has no certification from IGI, GIA, or GCAL, do not buy it.

